A||||20||Lisa 86 2m4||What's the difference between Fiero's?||||5||
Z||000000||Lisa 86 2m4||12-29-2000||09:19 PM||||Hi! I've had my Fiero for 9 years now, and only thought there were 2 kinds of Fiero's, my 2M4 and the 6 cyl GT.  Reading these boards I see 'formula', SE, GT, .... Can I still be educated after all this time?<BR>Thank you!!<BR>Lisa||||reg||5
Z||000001||Fformula88||12-29-2000||10:14 PM||||There aren't too many Fieros but a few variations of each model.  Going by model year, I'll try to quickly recap each one.<P>2m4's are 84-86 and are notchback and 4 cyl<P>2m6's are again 84-86 with V6 engine, also has Aero nose in 86<P>GT's  None in 84.  85 has Aero nose and is notchback, 86-88 has fastback bodystyle.  All V6<P>SE's can be 2m4 and 2m6, continued thru 87.  Basically an option package for coupes.<P>Formula was a performance option pkg replacing SE in lineup for 88.  Basically this car has the GT V6 engine, WS6 suspension with regular coupe/notchback body style.  Most also have far less options.<P>Hope this helps.  <P>I am sure others will add to my quick summaries.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">  <BR>1988 Fiero Formula||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||12-29-2000||10:19 PM||||84-88 Coupe = 4 cyl base car 87/88 had slightly different nose and rear bumper.<BR>84 Indy = same body style as 85 GT but only 4cyl available. only 2000 made.<BR>(no V-6's in 84)<BR>SE = 84/85 base body style, 85 had an optional V-6. Both had upgraded suspension and 14" wheels.<BR>85 GT and 86/87 SE = Had "areo" nose and ground effects.<BR>86-88 GT had the "fastback" body style<BR>88 Formula (no 88 SE) had V-6, GT style wheels, and coupe body.<P>As for transmissions,<BR>84 had 4-spd or auto<BR>85 4cyl had 5-spd or auto, V-6 had 4spd or auto<BR>86 V-6's got 5-spds late into the year.<BR>87-88 5spd's or auto.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 12-29-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||DaRkLoRD||12-29-2000||10:23 PM||||well, I think those posts pretty much cover the differences..<P>anyway, welcome to the forum.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000004||Raydar||12-29-2000||10:25 PM||||Lisa, Welcome to the forum!<BR>As for the body styles...<BR> The original notchback body style -84 2M4, 85 2M4 & 2M6, 86 (non SE)coupe. 87 and 88 coupe. 88 Formula.<BR> The Indy body style -84 Indy, 85 GT, 86 & 87 SE. Aero ground F/X, like a GT, on a notchback body. <BR> Fastback body style -86 thru 88 GT.<BR> The 87 and 88 coupes got different front and rear fascias (no black bumper pads) than the 84-86 models.<BR>The 88 (only year) Formula looks like a base 88 coupe, but has the GT running gear, and a wing. <BR>Hope this helps.<P>Raydar   ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||12-29-2000||10:29 PM||||Wow! Didn't we all jump on <I>that</I> question!<BR>Anyways... Welcome.||||reg||1
